{%- comment -%}
  alc-mirror-sizes — "On your wall" for LED mirror collections: the same to-scale
  chooser as the wall-art page (sections/alc-wall-art.liquid), with a bathroom wall.

  - Three steps: shape (rectangular, round, oval, polygonal), then the width the
    shape comes in (the diameter for round mirrors), then the heights of that
    width; each chip shows its number of models.
  - The wall (380 x 260 cm) shows the mirror to scale above the vanity it fits: the
    narrowest standard vanity (60/80/100/120/160 cm) at least as wide as the mirror,
    the mirror centred at eye level (160 cm) and at least 115 cm off the floor so it
    clears the tap.
  - Below, the models in that size, in-stock first (rendered from a JSON list, so a
    collection of 300+ mirrors does not ship hundreds of hidden cards).

  Sizes come from custom.lungime (width) and custom.inaltime (height), or
  custom.diametru for round mirrors; the shape from the title (Rotunda / Ovala /
  Poligon). "Ovala" mirrors are capsules, polygons are drawn as 12-sided.

  Shown on the first page of the collection only. UI text is in the per-language
  dictionary below. Styles: assets/alc-wall-art.css (shared chips, wall, strip) +
  assets/alc-mirror-sizes.css.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign lang = request.locale.iso_code | downcase | slice: 0, 2

  comment
    d: eyebrow | title | intro | shape | width (step 2) | rectangular | round | oval | polygonal |
       caption ([w] = vanity width) | drawn to scale | models in this size | sold out |
       fallback name | vanity label ([w]) | height (step 3) | diameter (step 2, round)
  endcomment
  case lang
    when 'en'
      assign d = 'On your wall|See the real size, not just the numbers.|Every mirror is drawn to scale above the vanity it fits, centred at eye level – 160 cm from the floor.|Shape|Width|Rectangular|Round|Oval|Polygonal|Fits a [w] cm vanity · centred at eye level|Drawn to scale|Models in this size|Sold out|LED mirror|[w] cm vanity|Height|Diameter'
    when 'hu'
      assign d = 'A te faladon|Lásd a valódi méretet, ne csak a számokat.|Minden tükör méretarányosan van megrajzolva a hozzá illő fürdőszobabútor fölé, szemmagasságban – 160 cm-re a padlótól.|Forma|Szélesség|Szögletes|Kerek|Ovális|Sokszögű|[w] cm-es bútorhoz illik · szemmagasságban|Méretarányos rajz|Modellek ebben a méretben|Elfogyott|LED-es tükör|[w] cm-es bútor|Magasság|Átmérő'
    when 'pl'
      assign d = 'Na Twojej ścianie|Zobacz prawdziwy rozmiar, nie tylko liczby.|Każde lustro narysowano w skali nad pasującą szafką łazienkową, na wysokości oczu – 160 cm od podłogi.|Kształt|Szerokość|Prostokątne|Okrągłe|Owalne|Wielokątne|Pasuje do szafki [w] cm · na wysokości oczu|Rysunek w skali|Modele w tym rozmiarze|Wyprzedane|Lustro LED|szafka [w] cm|Wysokość|Średnica'
    when 'el'
      assign d = 'Στον τοίχο σας|Δείτε το πραγματικό μέγεθος, όχι μόνο νούμερα.|Κάθε καθρέφτης είναι σχεδιασμένος υπό κλίμακα πάνω από το έπιπλο μπάνιου που του ταιριάζει, στο ύψος των ματιών – 160 cm από το πάτωμα.|Σχήμα|Πλάτος|Ορθογώνιοι|Στρογγυλοί|Οβάλ|Πολυγωνικοί|Ταιριάζει σε έπιπλο [w] cm · στο ύψος των ματιών|Σχέδιο υπό κλίμακα|Μοντέλα σε αυτό το μέγεθος|Εξαντλήθηκε|Καθρέφτης LED|έπιπλο [w] cm|Ύψος|Διάμετρος'
    when 'bg'
      assign d = 'На вашата стена|Вижте истинския размер, не само числата.|Всяко огледало е нарисувано в мащаб над подходящия шкаф за баня, на нивото на очите – 160 cm от пода.|Форма|Ширина|Правоъгълни|Кръгли|Овални|Многоъгълни|Подходящо за шкаф [w] cm · на нивото на очите|Рисунка в мащаб|Модели в този размер|Изчерпан|LED огледало|шкаф [w] cm|Височина|Диаметър'
    when 'it'
      assign d = 'Sulla tua parete|Guarda la misura reale, non solo i numeri.|Ogni specchio è disegnato in scala sopra il mobile bagno adatto, all’altezza degli occhi: 160 cm dal pavimento.|Forma|Larghezza|Rettangolari|Rotondi|Ovali|Poligonali|Adatto a un mobile da [w] cm · all’altezza degli occhi|Disegno in scala|Modelli in questa misura|Esaurito|Specchio LED|mobile [w] cm|Altezza|Diametro'
    when 'fr'
      assign d = 'Sur votre mur|Voyez la taille réelle, pas seulement les chiffres.|Chaque miroir est dessiné à l’échelle au-dessus du meuble de salle de bain qui lui convient, à hauteur des yeux – 160 cm du sol.|Forme|Largeur|Rectangulaires|Ronds|Ovales|Polygonaux|Convient à un meuble de [w] cm · à hauteur des yeux|Dessin à l’échelle|Modèles dans cette taille|Épuisé|Miroir LED|meuble [w] cm|Hauteur|Diamètre'
    when 'cs'
      assign d = 'Na vaší stěně|Podívejte se na skutečnou velikost, ne jen na čísla.|Každé zrcadlo je nakresleno v měřítku nad koupelnovou skříňkou, ke které se hodí, v úrovni očí – 160 cm od podlahy.|Tvar|Šířka|Obdélníková|Kulatá|Oválná|Mnohoúhelníková|Hodí se ke skříňce [w] cm · v úrovni očí|Nákres v měřítku|Modely v této velikosti|Vyprodáno|LED zrcadlo|skříňka [w] cm|Výška|Průměr'
    when 'sk'
      assign d = 'Na vašej stene|Pozrite si skutočnú veľkosť, nie iba čísla.|Každé zrkadlo je nakreslené v mierke nad kúpeľňovou skrinkou, ku ktorej sa hodí, v úrovni očí – 160 cm od podlahy.|Tvar|Šírka|Obdĺžnikové|Okrúhle|Oválne|Mnohouholníkové|Hodí sa ku skrinke [w] cm · v úrovni očí|Nákres v mierke|Modely v tejto veľkosti|Vypredané|LED zrkadlo|skrinka [w] cm|Výška|Priemer'
    when 'hr'
      assign d = 'Na vašem zidu|Pogledajte stvarnu veličinu, ne samo brojeve.|Svako je ogledalo nacrtano u mjerilu iznad kupaonskog ormarića kojem pristaje, u visini očiju – 160 cm od poda.|Oblik|Širina|Pravokutna|Okrugla|Ovalna|Poligonalna|Pristaje ormariću od [w] cm · u visini očiju|Crtež u mjerilu|Modeli u ovoj veličini|Rasprodano|LED ogledalo|ormarić [w] cm|Visina|Promjer'
    when 'de'
      assign d = 'An Ihrer Wand|Sehen Sie die echte Größe, nicht nur die Zahlen.|Jeder Spiegel ist maßstabsgetreu über dem passenden Waschtisch gezeichnet, auf Augenhöhe – 160 cm über dem Boden.|Form|Breite|Rechteckig|Rund|Oval|Polygonal|Passt zu einem [w]-cm-Waschtisch · auf Augenhöhe|Maßstabsgetreue Zeichnung|Modelle in dieser Größe|Ausverkauft|LED-Spiegel|Waschtisch [w] cm|Höhe|Durchmesser'
    else
      assign d = 'Pe peretele tău|Vezi mărimea reală, nu doar cifrele.|Fiecare oglindă e desenată la scară deasupra mobilierului pe care se potrivește, la nivelul ochilor – 160 cm de la podea.|Formă|Lungime|Dreptunghiulare|Rotunde|Ovale|Poligonale|Se potrivește pe un mobilier de [w] cm · la nivelul ochilor|Desen la scară|Modele în această mărime|Stoc epuizat|Oglindă LED|mobilier [w] cm|Lățime|Diametru'
  endcase
  assign t = d | split: '|'
  assign shape_ids = 'rect,round,oval,poly' | split: ','
  assign sid = 'alcms-' | append: section.id
-%}

{%- if current_page == 1 -%}
  {%- paginate collection.products by 250 -%}
    {%- liquid
      comment
        One pass: each product's key ("shape-WxH"), the format rows to sort
        ("<shape order><width><height>|key|shape|w|h"), and the product list for the JSON.
      endcomment
      assign rows = ''
      assign keys = ''
      assign avail = ''
      for p in collection.products
        assign key = ''
        assign wv = p.metafields.custom.lungime.value | first
        assign hv = p.metafields.custom.inaltime.value | first
        assign dv = p.metafields.custom.diametru.value | first
        assign w = 0
        assign h = 0
        if wv != blank and hv != blank
          assign w = wv | remove: 'cm' | strip | replace: ',', '.' | plus: 0 | round
          assign h = hv | remove: 'cm' | strip | replace: ',', '.' | plus: 0 | round
        elsif dv != blank
          assign w = dv | remove: 'cm' | strip | replace: ',', '.' | plus: 0 | round
          assign h = w
        endif
        if w > 0 and h > 0
          comment
            Shape, in this order, from data that is not translated: Shopify's standard
            shape (it alone marks the polygons, as heptagonal), then custom.forma_, then
            the size (a diameter only = round). The title is a last resort for the few
            mirrors with neither field.
          endcomment
          assign mo = p.metafields.shopify.shape.value | first
          assign sh_std = mo.system.handle | default: ''
          assign mo = p.metafields.custom.forma_.value | first
          assign fh = mo.system.handle | default: ''
          assign tl = p.title | downcase
          assign shape = ''
          if sh_std contains 'gon'
            assign shape = 'poly'
          elsif sh_std == 'oval' or fh == 'ovala'
            assign shape = 'oval'
          elsif sh_std == 'round' or fh == 'rotunda'
            if w == h
              assign shape = 'round'
            endif
          elsif sh_std != '' or fh != ''
            assign shape = 'rect'
          endif
          if shape == ''
            if tl contains 'poligon' or tl contains 'polygon' or tl contains 'sokszög' or tl contains 'wielok' or tl contains 'πολυγων' or tl contains 'многоъгъл'
              assign shape = 'poly'
            elsif tl contains 'oval' or tl contains 'owal' or tl contains 'ovál' or tl contains 'οβάλ' or tl contains 'овал'
              assign shape = 'oval'
            elsif w == h and wv == blank
              assign shape = 'round'
            else
              assign shape = 'rect'
            endif
          endif
          case shape
            when 'rect'
              assign so = '1'
            when 'round'
              assign so = '2'
            when 'oval'
              assign so = '3'
            else
              assign so = '4'
          endcase
          assign key = shape | append: '-' | append: w | append: 'x' | append: h
          assign w_pad = '000' | append: w | slice: -3, 3
          assign h_pad = '000' | append: h | slice: -3, 3
          assign row = so | append: w_pad | append: h_pad | append: '|' | append: key | append: '|' | append: shape | append: '|' | append: w | append: '|' | append: h
          unless rows contains row
            assign rows = rows | append: row | append: ';'
          endunless
        endif
        assign keys = keys | append: key | append: ';'
        if p.available
          assign avail = avail | append: '1;'
        else
          assign avail = avail | append: '0;'
        endif
      endfor
      assign formats = rows | split: ';' | sort
      assign key_list = keys | split: ';'
      assign avail_list = avail | split: ';'

      comment
        Per format: models and models in stock. Per shape: models, and the size to show
        first (most in stock). The shape shown first is the one with most in stock.
      endcomment
      assign f_counts = ''
      assign shape_stock = ''
      assign default_shape = ''
      assign best_shape_n = -1
      for sh in shape_ids
        assign total = 0
        assign stock = 0
        assign best_n = -1
        assign best_k = ''
        for row in formats
          assign parts = row | split: '|'
          if parts[2] != sh
            continue
          endif
          assign n = 0
          assign n_av = 0
          for k in key_list
            if k == parts[1]
              assign n = n | plus: 1
              if avail_list[forloop.index0] == '1'
                assign n_av = n_av | plus: 1
              endif
            endif
          endfor
          assign f_counts = f_counts | append: parts[1] | append: ':' | append: n | append: ':' | append: n_av | append: ';'
          assign total = total | plus: n
          assign stock = stock | plus: n_av
          if n_av > best_n
            assign best_n = n_av
            assign best_k = parts[1]
          endif
        endfor
        assign shape_stock = shape_stock | append: sh | append: ':' | append: total | append: ':' | append: best_k | append: ';'
        if total > 0 and stock > best_shape_n
          assign best_shape_n = stock
          assign default_shape = sh
        endif
      endfor
      assign shape_rows = shape_stock | split: ';'
    -%}

    {%- if formats.size > 1 -%}
      {{ 'alc-wall-art.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}
      {{ 'alc-mirror-sizes.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}

      <div class="alcwa alcms">
        <section class="page-width alcwa__sizes alcms__sizes" id="{{ sid }}">
          <div class="alcwa__sizes-grid alcms__grid">
            <div class="alcwa__sizes-head">
              <p class="alcwa__eyebrow">{{ t[0] }}</p>
              <h2 class="alcwa__title">{% render 'alc-nbsp', text: t[1] %}</h2>
              <p class="alcwa__intro">{{ t[2] | replace: ' – ', '&nbsp;– ' | replace: ' cm', '&nbsp;cm' }}</p>
            </div>

            <div class="alcms__steps">

              {%- liquid
                comment
                  The format shown first: its shape, width and height.
                endcomment
                for srow in shape_rows
                  assign sp = srow | split: ':'
                  if sp[0] == default_shape
                    assign dk = sp[2] | split: '-' | last | split: 'x'
                    assign default_w = dk[0]
                    assign default_h = dk[1]
                  endif
                endfor
              -%}
              <p class="alcms__label" id="{{ sid }}-shape"><span class="alcms__step" aria-hidden="true">1</span>{{ t[3] }}</p>
              <div class="alcwa__chips alcms__chips alcms__chips--shape" role="group" aria-labelledby="{{ sid }}-shape">
                {%- for srow in shape_rows -%}
                  {%- liquid
                    assign sp = srow | split: ':'
                    assign sh = sp[0]
                    assign total = sp[1] | plus: 0
                    if total == 0
                      continue
                    endif
                    case sh
                      when 'rect'
                        assign sl = t[5]
                      when 'round'
                        assign sl = t[6]
                      when 'oval'
                        assign sl = t[7]
                      else
                        assign sl = t[8]
                    endcase
                  -%}
                  <button
                    type="button"
                    class="alcwa__chip"
                    data-step="shape"
                    data-shape="{{ sh }}"
                    data-default="{{ sp[2] }}"
                    aria-pressed="{% if sh == default_shape %}true{% else %}false{% endif %}"
                  >
                    <span class="alcms__shape alcms__shape--{{ sh }}" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                    <span>{{ sl }}</span>
                    <span class="alcwa__chip-count">{{ total }}</span>
                  </button>
                {%- endfor -%}
              </div>

              <p class="alcms__label" id="{{ sid }}-w">
                <span class="alcms__step" aria-hidden="true">2</span>
                <span data-label-w data-text="{{ t[4] | escape }}" data-text-round="{{ t[16] | escape }}">
                  {%- if default_shape == 'round' %}{{ t[16] }}{% else %}{{ t[4] }}{% endif -%}
                </span>
              </p>
              <div class="alcwa__chips alcms__chips" role="group" aria-labelledby="{{ sid }}-w">
                {%- assign seen = '' -%}
                {%- for row in formats -%}
                  {%- liquid
                    assign parts = row | split: '|'
                    assign group = parts[2] | append: '-' | append: parts[3] | append: 'x'
                    assign marker = ';' | append: group
                    if seen contains marker
                      continue
                    endif
                    assign seen = seen | append: marker
                    assign n = 0
                    for k in key_list
                      assign kp = k | slice: 0, group.size
                      if kp == group
                        assign n = n | plus: 1
                      endif
                    endfor
                  -%}
                  <button
                    type="button"
                    class="alcwa__chip"
                    data-step="w"
                    data-shape="{{ parts[2] }}"
                    data-w="{{ parts[3] }}"
                    aria-pressed="{% if parts[2] == default_shape and parts[3] == default_w %}true{% else %}false{% endif %}"
                    {% if parts[2] != default_shape %}hidden{% endif %}
                  >
                    <span>{{ parts[3] }} cm</span>
                    <span class="alcwa__chip-count">{{ n }}</span>
                  </button>
                {%- endfor -%}
              </div>

              <div data-step-h{% if default_shape == 'round' %} hidden{% endif %}>
                <p class="alcms__label" id="{{ sid }}-h"><span class="alcms__step" aria-hidden="true">3</span>{{ t[15] }}</p>
                <div class="alcwa__chips alcms__chips" role="group" aria-labelledby="{{ sid }}-h">
                  {%- for row in formats -%}
                    {%- liquid
                      assign parts = row | split: '|'
                      assign fk = parts[1]
                      assign needle = ';' | append: fk | append: ':'
                      assign fc_all = ';' | append: f_counts
                      assign fc = fc_all | split: needle | last | split: ';' | first | split: ':'
                    -%}
                    <button
                      type="button"
                      class="alcwa__chip"
                      data-step="h"
                      data-key="{{ fk }}"
                      data-shape="{{ parts[2] }}"
                      data-w="{{ parts[3] }}"
                      data-h="{{ parts[4] }}"
                      data-av="{{ fc[1] }}"
                      aria-pressed="{% if parts[2] == default_shape and parts[3] == default_w and parts[4] == default_h %}true{% else %}false{% endif %}"
                      {% unless parts[2] == default_shape and parts[3] == default_w %}hidden{% endunless %}
                    >
                      <span>{{ parts[4] }} cm</span>
                      <span class="alcwa__chip-count">{{ fc[0] }}</span>
                    </button>
                  {%- endfor -%}
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>

            <figure class="alcwa__wall">
              <div class="alcwa__scene alcms__scene" data-scene role="img" aria-label="{{ t[10] | escape }}">
                <div class="alcwa__ruler alcms__ruler" aria-hidden="true">
                  {%- for cm in (1..5) -%}
                    {%- assign y = cm | times: 50 -%}
                    <span style="bottom: {{ y | times: 100.0 | divided_by: 250 }}%"><i>{{ y }}</i></span>
                  {%- endfor -%}
                </div>
                <div class="alcms__mirror" data-mirror>
                  <svg class="alcms__poly" viewBox="0 0 100 100" preserveAspectRatio="none" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
                    <polygon points="37,1 63,1 85,13 98,35 98,65 85,87 63,99 37,99 15,87 2,65 2,35 15,13" />
                  </svg>
                </div>
                <div class="alcwa__dim alcwa__dim--w" data-dim-w><span data-dim-w-label></span></div>
                <div class="alcwa__dim alcwa__dim--h" data-dim-h><span data-dim-h-label></span></div>
                <div class="alcms__vanity" data-vanity aria-hidden="true">
                  <span class="alcms__tap"></span>
                  <span class="alcms__basin"></span>
                  <span class="alcms__top"></span>
                  <span class="alcms__cabinet"><i data-vanity-label></i></span>
                </div>
              </div>
              <figcaption class="alcwa__caption">
                <span data-caption></span>
                <span class="alcwa__caption-tag">{{ t[10] }}</span>
              </figcaption>
            </figure>
          </div>

          <div class="alcwa__strip-wrap">
            <div class="alcwa__strip-head">
              <p class="alcwa__strip-title">{{ t[11] }}</p>
              <div class="alcwa__strip-nav">
                <button type="button" class="alcwa__nav" data-prev aria-label="{{ 'general.slider.previous_slide' | t | escape }}" disabled>
                  <svg aria-hidden="true" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M19 12H5M11 6l-6 6 6 6"/></svg>
                </button>
                <button type="button" class="alcwa__nav" data-next aria-label="{{ 'general.slider.next_slide' | t | escape }}">
                  <svg aria-hidden="true" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg>
                </button>
              </div>
            </div>
            <ul class="alcwa__strip" role="list" data-strip></ul>
          </div>
        </section>

        {%- liquid
          comment
            The models, in-stock first: [key, product path, image, name, price, compare price, in stock].
            Paths drop the parts every model shares: the CDN folder (data-cdn) and "/products/".
          endcomment
          assign cdn_base = ''
          for p in collection.products
            if p.featured_media
              assign probe = p.featured_media | image_url: width: 600
              if probe contains '/files/'
                assign cdn_base = probe | split: '/files/' | first | append: '/files/'
              endif
              break
            endif
          endfor
        -%}
        <script type="application/json" data-models="{{ sid }}" data-cdn="{{ cdn_base }}">
          [
          {%- assign first_item = true -%}
          {%- for pass in (1..2) -%}
            {%- for p in collection.products -%}
              {%- liquid
                assign k = key_list[forloop.index0]
                if k == blank
                  continue
                endif
                if pass == 1 and p.available == false
                  continue
                endif
                if pass == 2 and p.available
                  continue
                endif
                assign img = ''
                if p.featured_media
                  assign img = p.featured_media | image_url: width: 600
                  if cdn_base != '' and img contains cdn_base
                    assign img = img | remove_first: cdn_base | remove: '&width=600'
                  endif
                endif
                assign pu = p.url
                assign pre = pu | slice: 0, 10
                if pre == '/products/'
                  assign pu = pu | remove_first: '/products/'
                endif
                capture nm
                  render 'alc-ms-name', title: p.title, fallback: t[13]
                endcapture
                assign cmp = ''
                if p.compare_at_price > p.price
                  assign cmp = p.compare_at_price | money
                endif
              -%}
              {%- unless first_item %},{% endunless -%}
              {%- assign first_item = false -%}
              [{{ k | json }},{{ pu | json }},{{ img | json }},{{ nm | strip | json }},{{ p.price | money | json }},{{ cmp | json }},{% if p.available %}1{% else %}0{% endif %}]
            {%- endfor -%}
          {%- endfor -%}
          ]
        </script>

        <script>
          (function () {
            var root = document.getElementById('{{ sid }}');
            var data = document.querySelector('script[data-models="{{ sid }}"]');
            if (!root || !data) return;
            var models = [];
            try { models = JSON.parse(data.textContent); } catch (e) { return; }

            var T = {
              out: {{ t[12] | json }},
              caption: {{ t[9] | json }},
              vanity: {{ t[14] | json }}
            };
            // The bathroom wall in cm.
            var WALL_W = 380, WALL_H = 260, COUNTER = 85, EYE = 160, MIN_BOTTOM = 115;
            var VANITIES = [60, 80, 100, 120, 160];
            var scene = root.querySelector('[data-scene]');
            var mirror = root.querySelector('[data-mirror]');
            var vanity = root.querySelector('[data-vanity]');
            var vanityLabel = root.querySelector('[data-vanity-label]');
            var caption = root.querySelector('[data-caption]');
            var dimW = root.querySelector('[data-dim-w]'), dimWl = root.querySelector('[data-dim-w-label]');
            var dimH = root.querySelector('[data-dim-h]'), dimHl = root.querySelector('[data-dim-h-label]');
            var shapeChips = root.querySelectorAll('[data-step="shape"]');
            var widthChips = root.querySelectorAll('[data-step="w"]');
            var heightChips = root.querySelectorAll('[data-step="h"]');
            var heightStep = root.querySelector('[data-step-h]');
            var widthLabel = root.querySelector('[data-label-w]');
            var strip = root.querySelector('[data-strip]');
            var prev = root.querySelector('[data-prev]'), next = root.querySelector('[data-next]');
            var pct = function (v, of) { return (v / of * 100).toFixed(3) + '%'; };
            var labelBase = scene.getAttribute('aria-label');

            function draw(chip) {
              var shape = chip.getAttribute('data-shape');
              var w = +chip.getAttribute('data-w'), h = +chip.getAttribute('data-h');
              var v = VANITIES[VANITIES.length - 1];
              for (var i = 0; i < VANITIES.length; i++) { if (VANITIES[i] >= w) { v = VANITIES[i]; break; } }
              var bottom = Math.max(EYE - h / 2, MIN_BOTTOM);
              var left = (WALL_W - w) / 2;

              mirror.style.left = pct(left, WALL_W);
              mirror.style.width = pct(w, WALL_W);
              mirror.style.bottom = pct(bottom, WALL_H);
              mirror.style.height = pct(h, WALL_H);
              mirror.setAttribute('data-shape', shape);

              vanity.style.left = pct((WALL_W - v) / 2, WALL_W);
              vanity.style.width = pct(v, WALL_W);
              vanityLabel.textContent = v + ' cm';

              var round = shape === 'round' || (shape === 'poly' && w === h);
              dimW.style.left = pct(left, WALL_W);
              dimW.style.width = pct(w, WALL_W);
              dimW.style.bottom = pct(bottom + h + 7, WALL_H);
              dimWl.textContent = (round ? 'Ø ' : '') + w + ' cm';
              dimH.style.left = pct(left + w + 7, WALL_W);
              dimH.style.bottom = pct(bottom, WALL_H);
              dimH.style.height = pct(h, WALL_H);
              dimH.style.opacity = round ? '0' : '1';
              dimHl.textContent = h + ' cm';

              caption.textContent = T.caption.replace('[w]', v);
              scene.setAttribute('aria-label', labelBase + ': ' + dimWl.textContent + (round ? '' : ' × ' + h + ' cm') + ' · ' + T.vanity.replace('[w]', v));
            }

            var CDN = data.getAttribute('data-cdn') || '';
            function img(path, n) {
              var full = path.charAt(0) === '/' ? path : CDN + path;
              return /width=\d+/.test(full) ? full.replace(/width=\d+/, 'width=' + n) : full + (full.indexOf('?') > -1 ? '&' : '?') + 'width=' + n;
            }
            function srcset(path) {
              return [200, 300, 400, 600].map(function (n) { return img(path, n) + ' ' + n + 'w'; }).join(', ');
            }
            function href(path) {
              return path.charAt(0) === '/' ? path : '/products/' + path;
            }

            function esc(s) {
              return String(s).replace(/[&<>"]/g, function (c) { return { '&': '&amp;', '<': '&lt;', '>': '&gt;', '"': '&quot;' }[c]; });
            }

            function fill(key) {
              var html = '';
              models.forEach(function (m) {
                if (m[0] !== key) return;
                var media = m[2]
                  ? '<img src="' + esc(img(m[2], 400)) + '" srcset="' + esc(srcset(m[2])) + '" sizes="(min-width: 990px) 200px, 40vw" alt="" loading="lazy" width="600" height="600">'
                  : '';
                var price = m[6]
                  ? (m[5] ? '<span class="alcwa__card-sale">' + esc(m[4]) + '</span><s>' + esc(m[5]) + '</s>' : '<span>' + esc(m[4]) + '</span>')
                  : '<span class="alcwa__card-out">' + esc(T.out) + '</span>';
                html += '<li class="alcwa__card' + (m[6] ? '' : ' is-soldout') + '"><a href="' + esc(href(m[1])) + '" class="alcwa__card-link">'
                  + '<span class="alcwa__card-media">' + media + '</span>'
                  + '<span class="alcwa__card-name">' + esc(m[3]) + '</span>'
                  + '<span class="alcwa__card-meta">' + price + '</span></a></li>';
              });
              strip.innerHTML = html;
              strip.scrollLeft = 0;
              nav();
            }

            function nav() {
              var max = strip.scrollWidth - strip.clientWidth;
              prev.disabled = strip.scrollLeft <= 2;
              next.disabled = strip.scrollLeft >= max - 2;
              prev.parentNode.hidden = max <= 2;
            }

            function press(list, chip) {
              list.forEach(function (c) { c.setAttribute('aria-pressed', c === chip ? 'true' : 'false'); });
              // On phones each step is one swipeable row: bring the chosen chip into view.
              var row = chip.parentNode;
              if (row.scrollWidth > row.clientWidth) {
                var off = chip.getBoundingClientRect().left - row.getBoundingClientRect().left;
                if (off < 0 || off + chip.offsetWidth > row.clientWidth) row.scrollLeft += off - 24;
              }
            }

            // Step 3: the height decides the exact format.
            function selectHeight(chip) {
              press(heightChips, chip);
              draw(chip);
              fill(chip.getAttribute('data-key'));
            }

            // Step 2: the width shows the heights it comes in. It keeps the height
            // already chosen when the width has it, else takes the best-stocked one.
            function selectWidth(chip, keepH) {
              press(widthChips, chip);
              var shape = chip.getAttribute('data-shape'), w = chip.getAttribute('data-w');
              var pick = null, kept = null;
              heightChips.forEach(function (c) {
                var on = c.getAttribute('data-shape') === shape && c.getAttribute('data-w') === w;
                c.hidden = !on;
                if (!on) return;
                if (keepH && c.getAttribute('data-h') === keepH) kept = c;
                if (!pick || +c.getAttribute('data-av') > +pick.getAttribute('data-av')) pick = c;
              });
              if (kept || pick) selectHeight(kept || pick);
            }

            // Step 1: the shape shows its widths and opens on its best-stocked format.
            // Round mirrors have one number, so step 2 reads "diameter" and step 3 hides.
            function selectShape(chip) {
              press(shapeChips, chip);
              var shape = chip.getAttribute('data-shape');
              var dk = (chip.getAttribute('data-default') || '').split('-').pop().split('x');
              var want = null, first = null;
              widthChips.forEach(function (c) {
                var on = c.getAttribute('data-shape') === shape;
                c.hidden = !on;
                if (on && !first) first = c;
                if (on && c.getAttribute('data-w') === dk[0]) want = c;
              });
              var round = shape === 'round';
              heightStep.hidden = round;
              widthLabel.textContent = widthLabel.getAttribute(round ? 'data-text-round' : 'data-text');
              if (want || first) selectWidth(want || first, dk[1]);
            }

            var page = function (dir) { strip.scrollBy({ left: dir * strip.clientWidth, behavior: 'smooth' }); };
            prev.addEventListener('click', function () { page(-1); });
            next.addEventListener('click', function () { page(1); });
            strip.addEventListener('scroll', nav, { passive: true });
            window.addEventListener('resize', nav, { passive: true });
            shapeChips.forEach(function (c) { c.addEventListener('click', function () { selectShape(c); }); });
            widthChips.forEach(function (c) { c.addEventListener('click', function () {
              var cur = root.querySelector('[data-step="h"][aria-pressed="true"]');
              selectWidth(c, cur && cur.getAttribute('data-h'));
            }); });
            heightChips.forEach(function (c) { c.addEventListener('click', function () { selectHeight(c); }); });

            scene.classList.add('is-instant');
            var start = root.querySelector('[data-step="shape"][aria-pressed="true"]') || shapeChips[0];
            if (start) selectShape(start);
            requestAnimationFrame(function () { requestAnimationFrame(function () { scene.classList.remove('is-instant'); }); });
          })();
        </script>
      </div>
    {%- endif -%}
  {%- endpaginate -%}
{%- endif -%}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "ALC - Mirror sizes",
  "tag": "section",
  "class": "section",
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "To-scale size chooser for LED mirror collections: shapes, sizes, a bathroom wall with the matching vanity, and the models in each size. Shown on the first page of the collection. Text is translated in the section's own dictionary."
    }
  ],
  "presets": [
    {
      "name": "ALC - Mirror sizes"
    }
  ]
}
